<%# A RULE STILL FUNDING SOMETHING THAT STOPPED. Local: `suggestion`.

    §8's copy target: `Netflix stopped in October, the rule is still funding it`.

    THE FIGURE IS WHAT IT COSTS A PERIOD, not what the rule's column says: a $1,200 six-monthly
    premium and a $200 per-period rate are the same sentence to a user only once both are stated
    in the unit the money actually leaves in (`Budget#steady_ask`). The rule's own figure is
    printed beside it, because that is the number they will see on the edit form.

    THE PAGE DOES NOT DELETE. An item that stopped because the subscription was cancelled wants
    the rule gone; one that stopped because the card was replaced wants it kept. The panel cannot
    tell those apart from entry history, so it says what it sees and puts both doors on the row. %>
<p>
  <span class="font-medium text-gray-900"><%= suggestion.detail[:item_name] %></span> stopped on
  <%= suggestion.detail[:last_seen_on].strftime("%b %-d, %Y") %> — nothing for
  <%= pluralize(suggestion.detail[:periods_empty], "period") %> — and the rule is still funding it at
  <span class="tabular-nums"><%= number_to_currency(suggestion.amount) %></span> a period.
</p>

<p class="text-gray-500">
  The rule says <%= number_to_currency(suggestion.detail[:rule_amount]) %>
  <%= budget_rule_basis(suggestion.subject) %><% if suggestion.detail[:pool_name] %>, filling <%= suggestion.detail[:pool_name] %><% end %>.
  Keep it or delete it — nothing here decides that for you.
</p>
